          "path": "_m/g/c/w/g/ripley-castle-wp/ingilbys-by-t-j-holroyd-3a.png",
          "filename": "Ingilbys by T & J Holroyd (3a).png",
          "caption": "The subjects of this photograph are Wilhelmina Ingilby (Q76035691); Elizabeth (née Macdowall), Lady Ingilby Elizabeth Macdowall (Q75995058); Sir Henry John Ingilby, 1st Baronet (1790–1870) Sir Henry John Ingilby, 1st Bt. (Q75995060).\n\nPhotograph is by T &amp; J Holroyd of Harrogate. The photographers were brothers Thomas Holroyd (1821–1904) and James Holroyd (c.1825–1874). Thomas was a portrait and landscape painter, and James was a photographer, both from Harrogate, North Yorkshire, England. Although they were both credited, it was James who took most of the photographs.",
          "alt": "The subjects of this photograph are Wilhelmina Ingilby (Q76035691); Elizabeth (née Macdowall), Lady Ingilby Elizabeth Macdowall (Q75995058); Sir Henry John Ingilby, 1st Baronet (1790–1870) Sir Henry John Ingilby, 1st Bt. (Q75995060).\n\nPhotograph is by T &amp; J Holroyd of Harrogate. The photographers were brothers Thomas Holroyd (1821–1904) and James Holroyd (c.1825–1874). Thomas was a portrait and landscape painter, and James was a photographer, both from Harrogate, North Yorkshire, England. Although they were both credited, it was James who took most of the photographs.",
